IMPORT prelude
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g1-interpretation`
IMPORT `g1-art1-defined-terms`

-- g1-tests-art1.l4: tests of Article 1, with every expected value decided from the source (the consolidated text and the amending instruments) before the module was run.

§ `Part 1 — Interpretation: tests of Article 1`

§§ `The definition of "Minister", text by text`

-- The Table of Legislation History names the nine texts; the first constructor of the shared noun is the day before the first of them.
-- Expectations, from the instruments:
--   R&O.40/2019 Sch 2 para 1(e) substitutes "Minister for External Relations" for "Chief Minister" (made and in force 31 May 2019);
--   R&O.29/2021 Sch 2 para 1(e) substitutes "Minister for External Relations and Financial Services" for "Minister for External Relations" (2 March 2021);
--   R&O.28/2023 Sch 2 para 1(4) substitutes "Chief Minister" for "Minister for External Relations and Financial Services" (made 5 April 2023, in force 7 days after: 12 April 2023);
--   R&O.10/2024 Sch 4 para (1) substitutes "Minister for External Relations" for "Chief Minister" (at 9.30 a.m. on 27 February 2024);
--   R&O.102/2026 Art 1 substitutes "Chief Minister" for "Minister for External Relations" (made 25 September 2026, in force 7 days after: 2 October 2026).
#ASSERT REFUSED `Art 1 the Minister under the text of` `before the first consolidated version`
#ASSERT REFUSED `Art 1 the Minister under the text of` `before the first consolidated version` BECAUSE "no text of the Law before 1 January 2019 is among the sources"
#ASSERT `Art 1 the Minister under the text of` `the text of 1 January 2019` EQUALS `the Chief Minister`
#ASSERT `Art 1 the Minister under the text of` `the text of 31 May 2019` EQUALS `the Minister for External Relations`
#ASSERT `Art 1 the Minister under the text of` `the text of 16 December 2019` EQUALS `the Minister for External Relations`
#ASSERT `Art 1 the Minister under the text of` `the text of 1 January 2020` EQUALS `the Minister for External Relations`
#ASSERT `Art 1 the Minister under the text of` `the text of 2 March 2021` EQUALS `the Minister for External Relations and Financial Services`
#ASSERT `Art 1 the Minister under the text of` `the text of 12 April 2023` EQUALS `the Chief Minister`
#ASSERT `Art 1 the Minister under the text of` `the text of 27 February 2024` EQUALS `the Minister for External Relations`
#ASSERT `Art 1 the Minister under the text of` `the text of 16 October 2025` EQUALS `the Minister for External Relations`
#ASSERT `Art 1 the Minister under the text of` `the text of 2 October 2026` EQUALS `the Chief Minister`

-- The day 27 February 2024: the text changes at 9.30 a.m. (R&O.10/2024). An act at 08:00 is under the text of 12 April 2023 and an act at 10:00 under the text of 27 February 2024;
-- the vintage resolver chooses between them, and the two texts give different offices.
#ASSERT `Art 1 the Minister under the text of` `the text of 12 April 2023` EQUALS `the Chief Minister`
#ASSERT NOT (`Art 1 the Minister under the text of` `the text of 12 April 2023` EQUALS `Art 1 the Minister under the text of` `the text of 27 February 2024`)

-- The Order R&O.56/2025 under Article 2(2) was made by THE MINISTER FOR EXTERNAL RELATIONS on 9 October 2025, which is the office the text of 15 October 2025 (the text of 27 February 2024) names.
#ASSERT `Art 1 the Minister under the text of` `the text of 27 February 2024` EQUALS `the Minister for External Relations`

§§ `The chain of amendments closes`

-- Each amending instrument replaces the words the instrument before it put in. The table below is read off the five instruments, in the order of the Table of Legislation History.
DECLARE `Step in the amendment of the definition of Minister` HAS
    instrument IS A STRING
    `office replaced` IS AN `Office of the Minister`
    `office put in` IS AN `Office of the Minister`
    `text that results` IS A `Vintage of the text`

`R&O.40/2019 step` MEANS
    `Step in the amendment of the definition of Minister` WITH
        instrument IS "R&O.40/2019 Sch 2 para 1(e)"
        `office replaced` IS `the Chief Minister`
        `office put in` IS `the Minister for External Relations`
        `text that results` IS `the text of 31 May 2019`

`R&O.29/2021 step` MEANS
    `Step in the amendment of the definition of Minister` WITH
        instrument IS "R&O.29/2021 Sch 2 para 1(e)"
        `office replaced` IS `the Minister for External Relations`
        `office put in` IS `the Minister for External Relations and Financial Services`
        `text that results` IS `the text of 2 March 2021`

`R&O.28/2023 step` MEANS
    `Step in the amendment of the definition of Minister` WITH
        instrument IS "R&O.28/2023 Sch 2 para 1(4)"
        `office replaced` IS `the Minister for External Relations and Financial Services`
        `office put in` IS `the Chief Minister`
        `text that results` IS `the text of 12 April 2023`

`R&O.10/2024 step` MEANS
    `Step in the amendment of the definition of Minister` WITH
        instrument IS "R&O.10/2024 Sch 4 para (1)"
        `office replaced` IS `the Chief Minister`
        `office put in` IS `the Minister for External Relations`
        `text that results` IS `the text of 27 February 2024`

`R&O.102/2026 step` MEANS
    `Step in the amendment of the definition of Minister` WITH
        instrument IS "R&O.102/2026 Art 1"
        `office replaced` IS `the Minister for External Relations`
        `office put in` IS `the Chief Minister`
        `text that results` IS `the text of 2 October 2026`

-- Adjacent steps: what one puts in, the next replaces.
#ASSERT `R&O.40/2019 step`'s `office put in` EQUALS `R&O.29/2021 step`'s `office replaced`
#ASSERT `R&O.29/2021 step`'s `office put in` EQUALS `R&O.28/2023 step`'s `office replaced`
#ASSERT `R&O.28/2023 step`'s `office put in` EQUALS `R&O.10/2024 step`'s `office replaced`
#ASSERT `R&O.10/2024 step`'s `office put in` EQUALS `R&O.102/2026 step`'s `office replaced`

-- The chain starts from the words the first instrument replaced, which is the text of 1 January 2019, and ends at the line quoted from the consolidated text ("Minister" means the Chief Minister).
#ASSERT `R&O.40/2019 step`'s `office replaced` EQUALS `Art 1 the Minister under the text of` `the text of 1 January 2019`
#ASSERT `R&O.102/2026 step`'s `office put in` EQUALS `Art 1 the Minister under the text of` `the text of 2 October 2026`

-- Every text that an instrument produces is the office that instrument put in.
#ASSERT `R&O.40/2019 step`'s `office put in` EQUALS `Art 1 the Minister under the text of` (`R&O.40/2019 step`'s `text that results`)
#ASSERT `R&O.29/2021 step`'s `office put in` EQUALS `Art 1 the Minister under the text of` (`R&O.29/2021 step`'s `text that results`)
#ASSERT `R&O.28/2023 step`'s `office put in` EQUALS `Art 1 the Minister under the text of` (`R&O.28/2023 step`'s `text that results`)
#ASSERT `R&O.10/2024 step`'s `office put in` EQUALS `Art 1 the Minister under the text of` (`R&O.10/2024 step`'s `text that results`)
#ASSERT `R&O.102/2026 step`'s `office put in` EQUALS `Art 1 the Minister under the text of` (`R&O.102/2026 step`'s `text that results`)

-- The text before each step is the office that step replaced (the texts between the five steps that no instrument changes carry the office through).
#ASSERT `R&O.29/2021 step`'s `office replaced` EQUALS `Art 1 the Minister under the text of` `the text of 1 January 2020`
#ASSERT `R&O.28/2023 step`'s `office replaced` EQUALS `Art 1 the Minister under the text of` `the text of 2 March 2021`
#ASSERT `R&O.10/2024 step`'s `office replaced` EQUALS `Art 1 the Minister under the text of` `the text of 12 April 2023`
#ASSERT `R&O.102/2026 step`'s `office replaced` EQUALS `Art 1 the Minister under the text of` `the text of 16 October 2025`

§§ `The definition of "Comptroller", text by text`

-- L.13/2019 Sch 3 para 1 substitutes "Revenue Administration (Jersey) Law 2019" for "Income Tax (Jersey) Law 1961"; the Table of Legislation History gives 1 January 2020 (R&O.136/2019).
#ASSERT REFUSED `Art 1 the Law that defines the Comptroller under the text of` `before the first consolidated version`
#ASSERT `Art 1 the Law that defines the Comptroller under the text of` `the text of 1 January 2019` EQUALS `the Income Tax (Jersey) Law 1961`
#ASSERT `Art 1 the Law that defines the Comptroller under the text of` `the text of 31 May 2019` EQUALS `the Income Tax (Jersey) Law 1961`
#ASSERT `Art 1 the Law that defines the Comptroller under the text of` `the text of 16 December 2019` EQUALS `the Income Tax (Jersey) Law 1961`
#ASSERT `Art 1 the Law that defines the Comptroller under the text of` `the text of 1 January 2020` EQUALS `the Revenue Administration (Jersey) Law 2019`
#ASSERT `Art 1 the Law that defines the Comptroller under the text of` `the text of 2 March 2021` EQUALS `the Revenue Administration (Jersey) Law 2019`
#ASSERT `Art 1 the Law that defines the Comptroller under the text of` `the text of 12 April 2023` EQUALS `the Revenue Administration (Jersey) Law 2019`
#ASSERT `Art 1 the Law that defines the Comptroller under the text of` `the text of 27 February 2024` EQUALS `the Revenue Administration (Jersey) Law 2019`
#ASSERT `Art 1 the Law that defines the Comptroller under the text of` `the text of 16 October 2025` EQUALS `the Revenue Administration (Jersey) Law 2019`
#ASSERT `Art 1 the Law that defines the Comptroller under the text of` `the text of 2 October 2026` EQUALS `the Revenue Administration (Jersey) Law 2019`

§§ `The definition of "registered charity"`

`a company` MEANS LIST `a company`
`a bare record` MEANS LIST `an unincorporated body or association of persons`
`no kind` MEANS EMPTY

-- An entity with the given standing and kinds. Name, purposes and governors play no part in the definition.
GIVEN standing IS A `Standing on the register`
      kinds IS A LIST OF `Kind of entity`
GIVETH AN Entity
`an entity with` standing `and kinds` kinds MEANS
    Entity WITH
        name IS "Test Charity"
        `standing on the register` IS standing
        `kinds of entity` IS kinds
        `is a Jersey entity` IS TRUE
        governors IS EMPTY
        purposes IS EMPTY

-- "an entity entered for the time being in the general section or the restricted section of the register": those two standings, and no other.
#ASSERT `Art 1 the entity is a registered charity` (`an entity with` `entered in the general section` `and kinds` `a company`)
#ASSERT `Art 1 the entity is a registered charity` (`an entity with` `entered in the restricted section` `and kinds` `a company`)
#ASSERT `Art 1 the entity is a registered charity` (`an entity with` `entered in the general section` `and kinds` `a bare record`)
#ASSERT `Art 1 the entity is a registered charity` (`an entity with` `entered in the restricted section` `and kinds` `a bare record`)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 1 the entity is a registered charity` (`an entity with` `not on the register` `and kinds` `a company`)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 1 the entity is a registered charity` (`an entity with` `an applicant for registration` `and kinds` `a company`)

-- The historic section holds formerly registered charities: not "entered ... in the general section or the restricted section", so not a registered charity (Article 8(5)).
#ASSERT NOT `Art 1 the entity is a registered charity` (`an entity with` `formerly registered and entered in the historic section` `and kinds` `a company`)

-- "An entity entered": a body that falls within no sub-paragraph of Article 2(1) is not an entity, so it is not a registered charity whatever the register says.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 1 the entity is a registered charity` (`an entity with` `entered in the general section` `and kinds` `no kind`)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 1 the entity is a registered charity` (`an entity with` `entered in the restricted section` `and kinds` `no kind`)

-- The standing alone, for the rules that ask about a past standing (Article 2(10)).
#ASSERT `Art 1 the standing is that of a registered charity` `entered in the general section`
#ASSERT `Art 1 the standing is that of a registered charity` `entered in the restricted section`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 1 the standing is that of a registered charity` `not on the register`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 1 the standing is that of a registered charity` `an applicant for registration`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 1 the standing is that of a registered charity` `formerly registered and entered in the historic section`

§§ `The definition of "publish" (fork F1.5)`

-- "publish ... means publish in a manner that, in the opinion of the person publishing, is likely to bring the information or how the information may be obtained to the attention of the public or of those affected".
-- Reading A (taken): the opinion of the person publishing. Reading B: the manner's likelihood, judged objectively.

-- Made available; the publisher thinks the manner will reach the audience, and it will.
`published and expected to reach` MEANS
    `Facts about a publication` WITH
        `made available by the person in some manner` IS TRUE
        `the person publishing is of the opinion that the manner is likely to bring it to the attention of the public or of those affected` IS TRUE
        `the manner is in fact likely to bring it to the attention of the public or of those affected` IS TRUE

-- The discriminating case of F1.5: a notice posted only in a locked cabinet, which its publisher honestly believes adequate.
`a notice in a locked cabinet` MEANS
    `Facts about a publication` WITH
        `made available by the person in some manner` IS TRUE
        `the person publishing is of the opinion that the manner is likely to bring it to the attention of the public or of those affected` IS TRUE
        `the manner is in fact likely to bring it to the attention of the public or of those affected` IS FALSE

-- The converse: the publisher thinks the manner inadequate, though it would in fact reach the audience.
`a notice thought inadequate` MEANS
    `Facts about a publication` WITH
        `made available by the person in some manner` IS TRUE
        `the person publishing is of the opinion that the manner is likely to bring it to the attention of the public or of those affected` IS FALSE
        `the manner is in fact likely to bring it to the attention of the public or of those affected` IS TRUE

-- Nothing was made available to anyone: there is no publication, whatever the publisher thinks.
`nothing made available` MEANS
    `Facts about a publication` WITH
        `made available by the person in some manner` IS FALSE
        `the person publishing is of the opinion that the manner is likely to bring it to the attention of the public or of those affected` IS TRUE
        `the manner is in fact likely to bring it to the attention of the public or of those affected` IS TRUE

#ASSERT `Art 1 the information has been published` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 1 and 2` `published and expected to reach`
#ASSERT `Art 1 the information has been published` `the interpretation of Articles 1 and 2 with F1.5 read the other way` `published and expected to reach`

#ASSERT `Art 1 the information has been published` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 1 and 2` `a notice in a locked cabinet`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 1 the information has been published` `the interpretation of Articles 1 and 2 with F1.5 read the other way` `a notice in a locked cabinet`

#ASSERT NOT `Art 1 the information has been published` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 1 and 2` `a notice thought inadequate`
#ASSERT `Art 1 the information has been published` `the interpretation of Articles 1 and 2 with F1.5 read the other way` `a notice thought inadequate`

#ASSERT NOT `Art 1 the information has been published` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 1 and 2` `nothing made available`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 1 the information has been published` `the interpretation of Articles 1 and 2 with F1.5 read the other way` `nothing made available`

-- Each reading is a callable function of its own.
#ASSERT `Art 1 published on the opinion of the person publishing` `a notice in a locked cabinet`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 1 published on the likelihood of the manner` `a notice in a locked cabinet`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 1 published on the opinion of the person publishing` `a notice thought inadequate`
#ASSERT `Art 1 published on the likelihood of the manner` `a notice thought inadequate`

-- The other six forks do not touch "publish": setting any of them the other way leaves the answer as it was.
#ASSERT `Art 1 the information has been published` `the interpretation of Articles 1 and 2 with F1.1 read the other way` `a notice in a locked cabinet`
#ASSERT `Art 1 the information has been published` `the interpretation of Articles 1 and 2 with F1.2 read the other way` `a notice in a locked cabinet`
#ASSERT `Art 1 the information has been published` `the interpretation of Articles 1 and 2 with F1.4 read the other way` `a notice in a locked cabinet`
#ASSERT `Art 1 the information has been published` `the interpretation of Articles 1 and 2 with F1.8 read the other way` `a notice in a locked cabinet`

§§ `The definitions that are roles`

#ASSERT `Art 1 Commissioner` EQUALS `the Commissioner`
#ASSERT `Art 1 court` EQUALS `the court`
#ASSERT `Art 1 tribunal` EQUALS `the Charity Tribunal`
#ASSERT `Art 1 JFSC` EQUALS `the Jersey Financial Services Commission`
#ASSERT `Art 1 Comptroller` EQUALS `the Comptroller`
